    "body": "### Problem\n\nNormally, pressing 'van' in normal mode will select  the textobject closest to it..\n\n<img width=\"691\" height=\"200\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/505f2e06-3827-473f-9053-3a4404db2566\" />\n\n\nBut if I have executed V first to select a line.like \n\n<img width=\"672\" height=\"253\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0f29799-cbff-446b-abd8-95c5925e67d9\" />\n\n\nand ESC to cancel the select, \n\nthen pressing `van`, it will select the entire line\n\n<img width=\"657\" height=\"210\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/913926ff-c532-4e21-a884-66a5e9213d52\" />\n\nNormally, the word should still be selected, instead of the entire line of code.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAs above\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAs above\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 11.5\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nno\n\n### Installation\n\nbrew",
