        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "`van` as far as I know means \"node\".\nOpen the inspectree `:InspectTree` and switch to the buffer with your code via `<C-w>h` or `<C-w>l` \nNow move your cursor to something. In the Inspectree you see the current node. `van` selects everything in the corresponding node - i may be an if-statement, a string, a function, a block, a word or whatever.\n\nAs I said the context is important. `van` is non deterministic if you don't know what the current node is or in other words, what the semantic context of the node under the cursor is.",
            "created_at": "2026-09-01T18:05:50Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41598#issuecomment-5498247052",
